+// Key for a bound instance: its SECTION, not its fragment id. Superseding exists because one
+// section's code relocates through a single global section base; a second copy of the same
+// section at another base is what goes stale. Different sections never share that base, and
+// games reuse one fragment id for many sections that are live at once (Pokemon Stadium's
+// model slot, id 239: the rental/Pokedex/detail models), so keying by id unregistered models
+// still on screen (PSR issue #13). Section keys are tagged so they can't collide with the
+// no-bind path's id keys.
+static uint32_t live_range_key_for_section(size_t section_index) {
+    return 0x80000000u | (uint32_t)section_index;
+}
